    "body": "Lab: Codex. Class: native geometric development research / bounded learning, unadopted components.\n\nThe saved 18/20 native source realizer only transfers to 2/16 authored rows (14 distinct source/query inputs). This change adds fixed-weight source interventions and reuses the existing Rust learner for eight new multiword sources alongside the original twenty. It preserves the geometric context and ordinary Copy/Period/Stop answer loss.\n\nThe continuation reaches 20/20 original complete replies at updates16/32/48, but construction stays0/8 and development transfer2/16. Six construction prefixes improve; final64 regresses EOS and is retained as a negative. Preserve32/48 as unadopted component candidates. Next is existing context adaptation with the frozen data; it is NOT_RUN. No new cursor, transformer comparison, session edit or geometric-family rejection.\n\nValidation: both executed source revisions pass9 focused Rust tests and optimized builds on CPU-only Runpod. Transfer6.199s/zero updates; continuation305.301s/64 updates with fixed context. Independent reviews recompute3,268 training positions,220 generated rows/2,574 generation steps, all row regressions, aliases/ties and fixed payloads. All transfer10files/28.5MB and continuation135files/331.9MB returned and SHA/size verified. Python only supervises processes and checks report arithmetic. Metal unavailable onLinux, not counted; compatibility statuses are not test results.\n\nExecuted source commits6643af20 ande0117909 remain in ancestry. Delivery integrates main d87de5e6's unrelated stack/L2 changes without altering the executed example blob. Compile-only integration check at exact delivery head541a0bc9 passes (40.433s, exit0) for the merged dependencies; no model rerun is required for the unchanged native occurrence path. Complete work charged60min once, ledger1,064,235,028/1,130,000,000ms; runtime remains a replaying/allocating component wrapper, not full-serving or chat qualification.\n\nReferences #1552, #1512, #820.\n",
